From ddaa7e283e14ed9bdf7b20360cf641c4cda2d36b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fab <faibiantorrestech@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:11:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(website): re-read the browser url bar after a burst of
 events

A link opened in Firefox from another app fires its accessibility events
before the address bar exists, then goes quiet, so the landing page was
never checked against keyword groups. Re-read the bar 0.8s and 2.5s after
the last browser event, and fall back to a capped tree walk because the
system id lookup cannot find Firefox's Compose address bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AeXNKkBfqarSMLZWk676Bs
---
